<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-abu-hassun"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-abu-hassun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Abu Hassun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Abu Hassun was the last Wattasid ruler of Morocco.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-adil-shah-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Adil Shah I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Adil Shah I was the fifth Adil Shahi sultan of Bijapur, ruling from 1558 to 1580.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-adil-shah-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Adil Shah II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Adil Shah II ruled the Bijapur Sultanate from 1656 to 1672.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-al-mandri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-al-mandri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali al-Mandri</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali al-Mandri was a military leader from the Emirate of Granada who refounded Tetouan in northern Morocco around 1484, with Wattasid permission, rebuilding the ruined…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-al-rida"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-al-rida.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali al-Rida</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali al-Rida was the eighth Imam of Twelver Shia Islam, a descendant of the Prophet Muhamm