 class="enc-snip">Ali ibn Munqidh was the founder of the Munqidhite emirate of Shaizar on the Orontes in Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-rashid"><span class="enc-name">Ali ibn Rashid</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali ibn Rashid was a sharif of the Banu Rashid who founded Chefchaouen in the Rif mountains of Morocco in 1471.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-yusuf"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-ibn-yusuf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali ibn Yusuf</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali ibn Yusuf was the Almoravid ruler from 1106 to 1143, son of Yusuf ibn Tashfin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-iqbal-al-dawla"><span class="enc-name">Ali Iqbal al-Dawla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Iqbal al-Dawla was the ruler of the Taifa of Dénia from 1044 to 1076, son and successor of its founder Mujahid al-Amiri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-khamenei"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-khamenei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Khamenei</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Khamenei is an Iranian cleric who served as president of Iran from 1981 to 1989 and then succeeded Ruhollah Khomeini as Supreme Leader in 1989.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mardan-khan-bakhtiari"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mardan Khan Bakhtiari</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mardan Khan Bakhtiari was a chief of the Bakhtiari tribe who, after the fall of the Afsharids, seized Isfahan in 1750 and with Karim Khan Zand installed the young…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mirza-karkiya"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mirza Karkiya</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mirza Karkiya was a ruler of the Karkiya dynasty of Zaydi sayyids in eastern Gilan, on Iran's Caspian coast, with his seat at Lahijan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mohammed-khan"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mohammed Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mohammed Khan was the founder of Rohilla power in Rohilkhand, the region east of the upper Ganges.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mohsen-al-ahmar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-mohsen-al-ahmar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mohsen al-Ahmar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mohsen al-Ahmar is a Yemeni general, for decades one of the most powerful military commanders under President Ali Abdullah Saleh, from the same Sanhan tribe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-mughayat-syah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-mughayat-syah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Mughayat Syah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Mughayat Syah was the first sultan of Aceh in northern Sumatra, ruling from about 1514 until his death in 1530.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-murad-khan-zand"><span class="enc-name">Ali Murad Khan Zand</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ali Murad Khan Zand was a ruler of the Zand dynasty of Iran in the years after the death of Karim Khan Zand in 1779.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ali-nasir-muhammad"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ali-nasir-muhammad.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ali Nasir Muhamma